Root cause:
The bug was caused by the incorrect handling of memory pages that were marked as poisoned. Specifically, the previous implementation of `set_mce_nospec()` allowed for speculative access to these pages by using the `set_memory_uc()` function, which did not properly account for the state of the memory when the Virtual Machine Monitor (VMM) had unmapped the page. This led to potential faults or exceptions when the guest attempted to access a page that was no longer present, resulting in kernel Oops errors. The patch corrects this by ensuring that the poisoned page is marked as not-present (NP) and modifies the `set_mce_nospec()` function to always unmap the entire page, preventing speculative access and subsequent faults.
